VALIDATION / INTERPRETATION
- Bicycle and scooter are hypothetical representative ownership scenarios.
- Capital cost is depreciated using straight-line depreciation.
- Annual ownership costs are allocated over 150 university commuting days.
- Scooter electricity includes a 15% charging-loss allowance.
- Electricity price, useful life, residual value and maintenance costs are explicit assumptions.
- Electricity cost is expected to be very small relative to depreciation and maintenance.
